   "title": "Legacy Guidance: Handling Audit Log Gaps and Access Errors in Pre-Rotation OAuth",
   "content_summary": "Describes the historical behavior of the OAuth Service regarding credential rotation and its impact on audit logs and access control, prior to the introduction of automated propagation.",
   "content_body": "In earlier versions of the OAuth Service, credential rotation did not automatically propagate to the Permission Engine, often resulting in missing audit log entries or unexpected access denials. Users frequently encountered account lockouts or elevated privilege anomalies because the system relied on manual synchronization rather than real-time updates. To resolve these issues, administrators were required to manually trigger a credential rotation and perform a comprehensive access review. Note that certificate warnings and unexpected logouts were common symptoms of this propagation delay. The recommended workaround involved verifying permission updates through the legacy console before closing the ticket."
